data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":386,"item_id":"fc_066a1b303f9f4f48016adf76463d2081919bfe0ae87e25e148","output_index":0,"arguments":"{\"pointer\":\"/checks/complete_target_and_representations\",\"coverage\":\"assessed\",\"judgment\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"Independently compared the complete source target, both parameters and both hypotheses with the inspected exported type and actual definitions. Nat includes n=0; E is any subset of Euclidean R^n with precisely the required nonemptiness and compactness. W n has n+1 real coordinates with L2 distance; pack and the projections are inverse coordinate identifications, and cyl imposes exactly membership in E and 0≤t≤1. EuclideanSpace.dist_eq/dist_sq_eq confirm the source square-root sum metric (also checked inside T008/T010). Native dimH is exactly source D005's ENNReal supremum with the Borel structure; Hausdorff measure's covering formula has arbitrary countable sets and no normalization, with empty terms zero. Proof.lean:19-54 supplies the actual Hmeasure/Hnative conversion, including infinite-scale handling. The empty-set dimension convention agrees with native dimH_empty. T005 establishes finiteness and E=univ when n=0; T006 and the interval/isometric-embedding branch handle zero ambient or Hausdorff dimension without a positive-dimension hypothesis at P. Actual ULift conversions preserve covers, costs and dimension through checked isometries and image/preimage arguments; no unproved equivalence is needed. The implementation retains the upper-cover, slicing lower bound, and zero-dimension interval branches and assembles both inequalities. No target clause or domain restriction is lost.\",\"locations\":[\"/scope\",\"/endpoints\",\"/mechanical_summary\",\"/scope/full_target\",\"/scope/parameters\",\"/scope/hypotheses\",\"/endpoints/P/source\",\"/endpoints/P/actual\",\"/endpoints/P/correspondence\",\"/documents/0\",\"/documents/2\"]}}"}

